in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/math/bundle
in @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian

# @epistemologic/math/curvature — the discrete-curvature reading on
# the sheaf-Laplacian operator at the edge altitude.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# `sheaf_laplacian.mirror` already names the operator (Δ_F = δ*δ) and
# `lambda_zero` (the spectral gap). Topping et al. 2022 (arXiv:2111.14522)
# names a SECOND quantity computable from the same combinatorial data:
# the Balanced Forman curvature Ric(i,j) on each edge of the underlying
# graph. The spectral gap reads connectivity AT THE WHOLE; the
# Balanced Forman curvature reads bottleneck-ness PER EDGE.
#
# Both are discrete descendants of Riemannian curvature:
#
#   - Ollivier-Ricci (2009; J. Func. Anal. 256) — coarse Ricci via
#     1-Wasserstein on neighbour measures. Combinatorial; correct;
#     intractable for general graphs.
#   - Forman-Ricci (Forman 2003; Discrete Comput. Geom. 29) — combinatorial
#     Ricci via face contributions. Cheap; loses some content.
#   - Balanced Forman (Topping et al. 2022, §4 Definition 1) —
#     re-balanced Forman to match Ollivier within a constant factor.
#     Tractable AND faithful. The current frontier for graph-rewiring.
#
# This shard names the discrete realisation of "curvature on the sheaf
# Laplacian's underlying graph at one edge" — what Topping et al. 2022's
# SDRF algorithm (Algorithm 1) ranks edges by. The substrate already
# spoke of curvature in `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §6
# ("rank tensions by curvature"); this shard gives that obligation a
# substrate-altitude carrier.
#
# === Why this lives at math/, not at fate/ ===
#
# `@fate.minimize` (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §3.2) CONSUMES
# curvature to rank tensions for fracture emission. The math layer
# names the obligation; the consumer altitude differs. Same split as
# `sheaf_laplacian` vs `minimize` — math underneath, consumer at @fate.
#
# === Bridge action ===
#
#   balanced_forman(op: operator, edge: restriction) -> curvature
#     The Balanced Forman curvature Ric(i,j) on edge (i,j) of the
#     graph underlying the operator. Per Topping et al. 2022 §4
#     Definition 1, equation (3): when min{d_i, d_j} > 1,
#
#       Ric(i,j) = 2/d_i + 2/d_j − 2
#                + 2·|#_Δ(i,j)|/max{d_i, d_j}
#                + 2·|#_Δ(i,j)|/min{d_i, d_j}
#                + (γ_max)^{-1} · (|#_□^i| + |#_□^j|) / max{d_i, d_j}
#
#     where:
#       d_i, d_j           = degrees of i, j in the underlying graph;
#       |#_Δ(i,j)|         = number of triangles through edge (i,j);
#       |#_□^i|, |#_□^j|   = number of 4-cycles based at i, j (without
#                            diagonals);
#       γ_max(i,j)         = max number of 4-cycles based at i ~ j
#                            traversing a common node;
#       and the γ_max term is zero when |#_□^i| = |#_□^j| = 0.
#
#     The degenerate case min{d_i, d_j} = 1 yields Ric(i,j) := 0 per
#     Topping et al. 2022 Definition 1.
#
#     Negative curvature → edge behaves as a bridge between
#     neighbourhoods (bottleneck). Positive curvature →
#     neighbourhoods stay connected after edge removal. Bound:
#     Ric(i,j) > −2 (Topping et al. 2022 §4 Proposition 4).
#
#     The discrete realisation of `bundle.mirror`'s `holonomy` reading
#     localised to one edge: cycle-averaged holonomy IS Magnot's κ
#     (arXiv:2509.10536, 2025), and Balanced Forman is the per-edge
#     decomposition the same combinatorial substrate supports.
#
# === Floor types: substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `sheaf_laplacian.mirror`'s precedent (eigenvalue carrier wraps a
# `ref` plus a multiplicity cardinal), the `curvature` carrier wraps a
# `ref` for the scalar value plus an `edge` field that records WHICH
# edge the value applies to. This shape lets a consumer collect the
# per-edge curvature map without losing the edge identity — load-bearing
# for `@fate.minimize`'s "rank tensions by curvature" step.
#
# === The substrate-pull recognitions this surfaces ===
#
# 1. The 19th-instance pattern (per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]):
#    `bundle.mirror`'s `holonomy` already names cycle-averaged curvature
#    at the bundle altitude; `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `eigen_d` already
#    names the operator-spectrum reading. This shard's `curvature` is
#    the per-edge localisation of `holonomy` — the substrate was
#    speaking of curvature; it now has the type name at the eigenboard
#    altitude.
#
# 2. The SDRF reading IS the per-edge form of "rank by curvature": the
#    same algorithmic shape `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §6 named
#    in the spec already, now declared at the math altitude one floor
#    beneath `@fate.minimize`.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Each type and action below names an established object older than
# the discipline of computer science (or younger but pre-LLM):
#
#   curvature           Riemann 1854 (Über die Hypothesen, welche der
#                       Geometrie zu Grunde liegen); Ricci 1903.
#   balanced_forman     Topping et al. 2022, arXiv:2111.14522
#                       (re-balancing of Forman 2003, Discrete Comput.
#                       Geom. 29:323-374; itself a descendant of Forman's
#                       1949-onward combinatorial topology work).
#   triangle_count      Wiener 1947 (path-counting in graphs);
#                       Erdős-Rényi 1959 (extremal triangle theory).
#   four_cycle_count    Bondy-Simonovits 1974 (Z₂ₖ-free graphs);
#                       Caccetta-Häggkvist 1978.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-edge curvature
# read so the eigenboard's numerical realisation has a substrate-altitude
# home alongside the spectral-gap reading. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md §3.2
#               ("rank tensions by curvature"); §6 (the SDRF Algorithm 1
#               transfer); arXiv:2111.14522 §4 Definition 1 (the exact
#               formula); arXiv:2111.14522 §4 Algorithm 1 (the ranking
#               step Reed's lean wires `@fate.minimize` to consume).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (curvature is its own
#                      newtype; the scalar lives in a typed carrier
#                      alongside the edge it reads),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (the
#                      19th-instance recognition: bundle.holonomy and
#                      spectral-triple.spectrum already implied this).
# Related shards: shards/epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror
#                 (the operator family this shard's curvature reads),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror
#                 (the abstract (A, H, D) triple whose discrete
#                 realisation is what this shard reads curvature on),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (the
#                 principal-G tower whose holonomy IS the cycle-averaged
#                 form of this shard's per-edge curvature).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/curvature.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/math/curvature` per the
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace` rule.

prism @epistemologic/math/curvature {
  focus curvature
  project curvature
  split curvature
  shift curvature
  settle curvature
}

# === The curvature carrier ===
#
# The Balanced Forman curvature read on one edge of the operator's
# underlying graph. Carries both the scalar value (a `ref` per the
# substrate's float-valued floor) and the edge it reads — so a
# consumer collecting the per-edge curvature map can rank without
# losing edge identity.
#
# `value` carries the curvature scalar as a `ref` (matches
# `sheaf_laplacian.eigenvalue.value`'s precedent).
# `edge` carries the source restriction the value applies to (the
# substrate's `restriction` type from `sheaf_laplacian.mirror`).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (value, edge). The realisation
# layer enforces this; the substrate names it.
#
# Audible register: a curvature is the per-step bottleneck reading on
# one voice-leading step. Negative curvature is a leap (long-distance
# pull between sparse neighbourhoods); positive curvature is a step
# (the neighbourhoods stay connected if you remove the leap).
type curvature = {
  value: ref,
  edge:  restriction,
}

# === balanced_forman — the per-edge Balanced Forman curvature ===
#
# Computes Ric(i,j) per Topping et al. 2022 §4 Definition 1, equation
# (3) on the edge `edge` of the graph underlying `op`. The substrate
# names the obligation; the FFI body (boundary Rust) discharges the
# combinatorial count.
#
# `@fate.minimize` (per `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` §3.2 and §6)
# ranks tensions by curvature for fracture emission: SDRF Algorithm 1's
# step 1 selects the edge with MINIMAL Ric(i,j) as the rewrite target.
# This action is the per-edge primitive that ranking step consumes.
#
# Pure; no I/O; deterministic per IEEE-754 floating-point semantics on
# the platform.
balanced_forman(op: operator, edge: restriction) -> curvature { \ }

out @epistemologic/math/curvature
out curvature
out balanced_forman
